															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dankaar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1790336); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1790336&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607805655" alt="dankaar" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1790336)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dankaar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1790336); return false;" >dankaar</a></span> <span class="odate time_1438617114 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Aug 2015 15:51</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2351121">
									

<p>My first SCP is here!</p>
<p>I'd like to thank everyone who took a peek at this draft, both in the forums and chat, you guys really helped me flesh this thing out.</p>
<p><strong>Spoilers</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">What's&nbsp;going&nbsp;on?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I&nbsp;know&nbsp;what's&nbsp;going&nbsp;on!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The term &quot;Yggdrasil-Severence event&quot; is the major clue here. For those not in the know, &quot;Yggdrasil&quot; was the name of the World Tree in Norse mythology, which held all the various realms together. The term is, essentially, <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ExactlyWhatItSaysOnTheTin">exactly what it says on the tin</a>.<br />
The knife here, in the process of creating a rift to another universe, severs the bonds that connect that universe to the rest of the Multiverse. Without these bonds, the laws of reality in those universes start to really go wild, and will almost always end up inhospitable to life as we know it, if not outright destroy that universe.<br />
Since the laws of reality get screwed up, so does anything in there, whether or not they're native to that universe. Hence the Bad Stuff that happened to the D-Class and the drones.<br />
&#8230; And yes, that letter is indeed a standard form, since this sort of things happens an infinite amount of times in an infinite multiverse. Just easier to print out a standard form and fill in the blanks than to write up a new one each time it occurs.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+The&nbsp;Hallway</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;The&nbsp;Hallway</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>If you already read the above, then you don't need me to tell you that the D-class isn't the only one suffering from &quot;can't reach my destination!&quot; syndrome. What's going on there is that Zeno's Paradox of the Tortoise and Achilles has more-or-less become a Real Thing. Anyone/anything trying to get to anywhere must reach the halfway point. And to get there, they have to reach the halfway point of that, and so on, and so on. The end effect is that they can never reach their destination, no matter how fast or how much they move.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+The&nbsp;Eclipse</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-The&nbsp;Eclipse</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>That's Mercury, and gravity from other worlds have gotten a LOT stronger.<br />
Also, a Level C PPE is basically a &quot;moonsuit&quot;, but takes in air from the outside and runs it through a powered air filtration system. <em>Of course</em> people will be staring at that D-Class!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+The&nbsp;Farm</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-The&nbsp;Farm</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Life is no longer possible in that universe, but that universe only realizes it when the wind carries the news.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Frozen</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Frozen</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Another one of Zeno's Paradoxes have largely become a Real Thing. In this case, the Paradox of the Arrow. In this instance, in any (duration-less) instance of time, no movement occurs as an object doesn't move from where it &quot;is&quot; to where it &quot;isn't&quot;. Therefore, even if you stitch all those instances of time together, movement isn't possible, since no movement occurs in any given instance.<br />
Note that this doesn't apply to, say, thinking. Which the D-Class (and everyone else in that universe) are more than capable of doing in their frozen state. And yes, there's a brief delay before that law applies to anything coming into that universe.<br />
Finally, the Foundation quit using D-class because they were losing them at a rate of one D-class for every two tests. Drones are probably cheaper at that point.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Melting</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Melting</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Bad news: It takes a lot less energy (heat) to transform a solid to a liquid.<br />
Good news: People can live as puddles! Wait, wait, that's still not good news&#8230; The larger the object is, however, the faster it melts.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+[No&nbsp;Signal]</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-[No&nbsp;Signal]</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Those [No Signal] patches are places where that universe doesn't exist anymore. It reads as [No Signal] because that's what happens if the monitors the Foundation uses aren't receiving data. Anything that touches those [No Signal] patches basically gets erased from existence.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

